# Backend settings. Copy to .env.local for the Convex CLI; never commit real values.

# ---- Which deployment the CLI talks to (one block) ----
# Local dev (no account): `CONVEX_AGENT_MODE=anonymous npx convex dev` writes these itself.
# CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=anonymous:anonymous-backend
# Self-hosted on loganserver (today's production), over the SSH tunnel in DOCUMENTATION.md §14:
# CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3299
# CONVEX_SELF_HOSTED_ADMIN_KEY=        # ssh loganserver cat foodsafe/.admin_key
# Convex Cloud (planned production, docs/issues/hosting-and-backups.md): `npx convex dev` after logging in
# writes CONVEX_DEPLOYMENT=dev:<name>; deploys use a deploy key from the Convex dashboard:
# CONVEX_DEPLOY_KEY=prod:...

# ---- Set ON the deployment, not here: npx convex env set NAME value ----
# BILLING_ENFORCED=true          Unlicensed businesses go read-only (convex/lib/licence.ts). Leave unset until
#                                billing is live and existing businesses have been given licences.
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_   From Stripe → Developers → Webhooks, for
#                                https://app.jampacked.co.nz/http/stripe/webhook (convex/http.ts). Until it's
#                                set the webhook answers 503 and Stripe retries.
# SEED_ALLOWED=true              Lets seed:run wipe everything and build docs/test-accounts.md. Pre-launch only.
# CLERK_JWT_ISSUER_DOMAIN=       Once Clerk is set up (docs/issues/clerk-authentication.md): the issuer URL
#                                for convex/auth.config.ts. Don't add auth.config.ts before this is set,
#                                or deploys fail.
